Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:40:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] mac80211: backport ath11k and mac80211 fixes from
 OpenWrt main

Take the patch files that OpenWrt main added after our base
98b1185d03 for the drivers this board uses, unchanged:

  ath11k 102-118 (from main fe0aacd956 "mac80211: ath11k: backport 17
    upstream fixes"): NULL dereference in ahb remove when QMI init is
    incomplete, PM notifier and reg_info leaks on init failure,
    dp_srng_setup leak, rx_tid locking, IDR mutation during mgmt TX
    cleanup, WMI TLV/CSA overreads, regulatory phy_id validation,
    out-of-range rx MCS
  ath11k 954-956 and subsys 484-490 (from main 24c13d794c "mac80211:
    backport nine upstream fixes"): unbalanced IRQ enable/disable,
    short management RX frames, ext IRQ setup leak; mac80211
    use-after-frees on station/chanctx teardown and an oversized
    fragment extra_len overflow a peer can trigger

The upstream commits also refresh other patch files for offsets that
depend on intermediate upstream changes, so only the new files are
taken. The whole mac80211 patch set (including 960/961 of this
project) applies to the pristine backports-7.2 tarball with no
rejects and no fuzz.
